        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harry Beaumont, Theodore Wharton\n- Films: Rose of the World, How Rastus Gets His Turkey\n- Companies: Fox, Goldwyn, Metro, Warner Brothers, Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer\n- Roles: film director, actor, screenwriter, producer, writer\n\nFacts:\n- Theodore Wharton (1875–1931) was an American film director, producer, and writer.\n- How Rastus Gets His Turkey is a 1910 slapstick comedy silent film directed by Theodore Wharton.\n- Harry Beaumont (February 10, 1888 – December 22, 1966) was an American film director, actor, and screenwriter.\n- Rose of the World is a 1925 American silent melodrama directed by Harry Beaumont and starring Patsy Ruth Miller, Allan Forrest, and Pauline Garon.\n- Harry Beaumont worked for Fox, Goldwyn, Metro, Warner Brothers, and Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.",
